(Bug #61 - a pad width past i32::MAX was read with `parse::<i32>()` and the
 Err was dropped by an `if let` with no else arm, so the width vanished and
 the value printed exactly as `{n}` would: no padding, no diagnostic, and a
 cliff between two adjacent literals. LANGUAGE.md:3107 puts no ceiling on
 the width and none is intended - `{n:2147483648}` now pads - so the only
 width that can be refused is one too large to hold, and it is refused out
 loud rather than dropped.)

a number called n is 255.
Print "{n:99999999999999999999}".
